# Guard files that predate the `@falsified-at:` requirement (2026-08-26).
#
# A guard that passes on the build it was written for proves nothing, and four distinct
# ways that happens turned up in one afternoon (QUALITY.md § B6m).  Every NEW file under
# tests/scripts/ therefore has to record the control it was falsified against —
#   // @falsified-at: <ref> — <which channel moved, with the numbers>
# — or say why it cannot have one:
#   // @falsified-at: none — <the reason>
#
# Produce the line with `scripts/falsify.sh <guard.loft> <control-ref>`, which runs the
# guard on both trees through the entry point the corpus runner picks and names the
# channel that moved.  Gated by `doc_hygiene::every_new_guard_records_its_control`.
#
# This list is a RATCHET, not a target: it only ever shrinks.  Retrofitting one is
# running the tool against the commit that fixed it and deleting the line here.
#
